WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.405
Welcome to Module 2 of the
Attribute-Driven Migration learning path:

2
00:00:04.405 --> 00:00:06.238
write a validation kit check.

3
00:00:06.238 --> 00:00:10.197
Every gate in the implementation
guide ends with a Validate step,

4
00:00:10.197 --> 00:00:12.837
and most of them name
a validation kit check.

5
00:00:12.837 --> 00:00:15.900
The kit is the executable
form of those steps.

6
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:21.605
This module serves Gate 3, and takes
Chapter 03 of the Federal Modernization

7
00:00:21.605 --> 00:00:24.865
Workbook's Book 19,
which teaches how a check

8
00:00:24.865 --> 00:00:28.125
is built through one new
check, V K SYNC oh two.

9
00:00:28.125 --> 00:00:31.982
It asks whether soft match and
hard-match takeover are blocked,

10
00:00:31.982 --> 00:00:34.800
and if not, whether an
approved window says why.

11
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:39.438
You'll see the parts of a check, its three
severities, why a missing value reads

12
00:00:39.438 --> 00:00:44.075
as off, and why a read-only check still
has to ask for the least privilege it can.

13
00:00:44.075 --> 00:00:48.737
Then you'll run it on the kit's fixtures
and on an export, and break it on purpose.

14
00:00:48.737 --> 00:00:49.990
Nothing signs in.
